@ai-craft/harness-audit

Portions of this package (the scoring engine types, scanner, scorer, report
renderers, the 36 `core` check pack checks, and the harness-detection support
modules) are ported from harness-score:

  https://github.com/paladini/harness-score
  Copyright (c) 2026 Fernando Paladini
  MIT License

The full upstream license text is included at
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/harness-score-LICENSE.

Trivial, contract-preserving differences from upstream (naming/module
boundaries only — check pass/fail semantics are unchanged):
  - The check catalog is organized as a `core` check pack
    (`{ id: 'core', checks: Check[] }`) rather than a flat `ALL_CHECKS` array,
    to make room for the pack/config extension layer planned for a later
    phase.
  - `GateMode` / `ResolvedScanConfig` / `ExtraRootEntry` live in a local
    `scan-config.ts` (types + a default only) instead of upstream's
    `config.ts`, since the `.harness-audit.json` file-driven config loader is
    a later phase, not this port.
  - The terminal/Markdown report renderers omit upstream's baseline-diff
    section (`ReportDiff` / `diff.ts`) — a CLI-only concern out of scope for
    this package's programmatic core engine.
